cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SceneGrid: Audio Observability & Runtime Platform"
message: "If you use SceneGrid in your research or software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Igor
    family-names: Zabrodin
    alias: rapt0p7
repository-code: "https://github.com/rapt0p7/scenegrid-console"
url: "https://github.com/rapt0p7/scenegrid-console"
abstract: >-
  SceneGrid is an enterprise-grade, observability-first runtime audio engine and
  middleware platform for the web. Built on Hexagonal Architecture (Ports and
  Adapters) and Data-Oriented Design (DOD), it provides zero-allocation voice
  pooling, deterministic polyphony culling with hysteresis, VCA-based mixer
  snapshots, predictive AudioWorklet sidechain ducking, gapless chunked audio
  streaming, ahead-of-time (AOT) static signal-graph validation, and real-time
  visual telemetry via an isolated inspector and Model Context Protocol (MCP)
  server.
keywords:
